{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And as for Ishmael, I have heard you, etc.</b> The intention is that Abraham did not pray for Ishmael except because he alone was his seed; once HaShem gave him seed from Sarah, he would no longer plead anymore on Ishmael's behalf. Therefore the Holy One, blessed be He, said to him: ״וּלְיִשְׁמָעֵאל שְׁמַעְתִּיךָ״ — meaning, I have accepted your words. This is along the lines of what they said, of blessed memory (Makkot 11a): the curse of a sage, even if conditional, is fulfilled, and the measure of good is greater than the measure of, etc. And according to what I explained, that Abraham's prayer for Ishmael was that he be a righteous man, HaShem hinted to him that he would return in repentance, as He said: ״הִנֵּה בֵּרַכְתִּי אוֹתוֹ״ — that he would return in repentance, for blessing means being included in the Blessed One, and the Blessed One is the source of holiness. And He used the past tense, <b>בֵּרַכְתִּי</b>, etc. — this is what He hinted at by saying (Genesis 15:15): ״תִּקָּבֵר בְּשֵׂיבָה טוֹבָה״, and so it was, as they said, of blessed memory (Genesis Rabbah 59:7), that he repented."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:41:45.312635087Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}